<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Byzantine–Sasanian War of 602–628</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/602">602</a>–<a href="/years/628">628 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Byzantine-Sasanian War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Byzantine-Sasanian War of 602–628 CE was the last and most destructive war between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>. Sasanian armies under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khosrow-ii">Khosrow II</a> conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraclius">Heraclius</a> counter-attacked and won at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nineveh">Nineveh</a> in 627. The war exhausted both powers and left them vulnerable to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/early-muslim-conquests">Arab conquests</a> that soon destroyed the Sasanian state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/byzantine-sasanian-war-of-602-628.jpg" alt="Byzantine–Sasanian War of 602–628" width="320" height="148" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Piero della Francesca · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Piero_della_Francesca_021.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
